WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:04.216
Upgrade Advisor is a read-only risk assessment, not an upgrade

00:00:04.224 --> 00:00:08.312
executor. For Cluster A, enter the intended current and target

00:00:08.363 --> 00:00:12.707
versions. Use saved PE and optional PC credential references

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.536
for the supported inventory reads.

00:00:14.582 --> 00:00:17.319
Keep certificate verification selected by default.

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:21.656
The PE and PC inventory controls have separate request-scoped TLS

00:00:21.665 --> 00:00:26.064
settings. An administrator can make a deliberate temporary exception where
permitted.

00:00:26.298 --> 00:00:30.471
The exception is audited and retained with collection results, and verification

00:00:30.564 --> 00:00:34.908
resets afterward. It does not change recovery health, drift or other

00:00:34.916 --> 00:00:36.423
workflows' trust settings.

00:00:36.686 --> 00:00:40.497
Review what the collection actually returned and what remains Unknown.

00:00:40.654 --> 00:00:43.249
A failed read is not a version value.

00:00:43.427 --> 00:00:47.174
NCC, LCM prechecks, firmware, Foundation

00:00:47.352 --> 00:00:51.002
and compatibility evidence are not all collected automatically.

00:00:51.169 --> 00:00:55.179
Supply missing information through the appropriate independent procedure and
retain

00:00:55.179 --> 00:00:58.542
its source. Run the assessment and open each finding.

00:00:58.763 --> 00:01:02.851
Check its source, affected version or feature, severity and recommended

00:01:02.902 --> 00:01:07.227
action. A saved declaration that release notes or compatibility were

00:01:07.227 --> 00:01:10.035
reviewed is not an automatic vendor check.

00:01:10.213 --> 00:01:14.522
Resolve the finding through its documented evidence, not by changing a label to look

00:01:14.522 --> 00:01:18.380
ready. Save the assessment snapshot with its inputs, collection

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:20.407
provenance and findings.

00:01:20.649 --> 00:01:23.649
Reassess when the target or evidence changes.

00:01:23.935 --> 00:01:28.481
Use the result alongside the vendor upgrade process and site change approval.

00:01:28.692 --> 00:01:32.996
It does not certify every hardware combination or submit an upgrade.
